WEBVTT

00:00:02.942 --> 00:00:04.113
(squeaks)

00:00:05.048 --> 00:00:07.549
Okay. Obviously, this is a lot,

00:00:07.684 --> 00:00:09.747
and you should be able to open
up about this on your own time,

00:00:09.883 --> 00:00:11.787
but we'll have plenty of time
to work through this

00:00:11.922 --> 00:00:13.354
on the way to Mount Rageous.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.450
(chuckles): Whoa. I am not
going to Mount Rageous.

00:00:15.585 --> 00:00:17.189
And neither are you, silly.

00:00:17.325 --> 00:00:19.755
You're never gonna leave again.

00:00:21.832 --> 00:00:22.995
Wait, what was the...

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.463
What was that last thing?

00:00:24.598 --> 00:00:26.669
Okay, guys,
if we're gonna save Floyd,

00:00:26.804 --> 00:00:27.802
we need to get going.

00:00:27.937 --> 00:00:28.968
I'll go get Poppy.

00:00:29.104 --> 00:00:30.436
No, no, no, wait. Hold on.

00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:32.338
There's no way
Viva's gonna let her go.

00:00:32.473 --> 00:00:34.276
What?
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:00:34.412 --> 00:00:36.477
Like I said, she's got
some stuff going on, man.

00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:39.911
If we don't want to get trapped,
we should sneak out now.

00:00:40.046 --> 00:00:42.481
(clunking)

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:47.255
(Rhonda roaring)

00:00:49.323 --> 00:00:51.858
(chuckling):
Ah, hey, Viva.

00:00:51.993 --> 00:00:53.256
What's up, girl?

00:00:53.391 --> 00:00:54.857
Viva, what are you doing?

00:00:54.993 --> 00:00:57.661
You're not leaving here,
no matter what, because...

00:00:57.796 --> 00:00:59.767
because it's just not safe
out there.

00:00:59.903 --> 00:01:00.836
You're welcome.

00:01:00.971 --> 00:01:02.136
Wait, is this about the Bergens?

00:01:02.272 --> 00:01:04.169
Because they stopped
trying to eat us.

00:01:04.304 --> 00:01:05.536
That's all in the past.

00:01:05.672 --> 00:01:07.204
Yeah, right.
That's hilarious, Poppy.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.403
I'm laughing really hard.

00:01:08.538 --> 00:01:09.871
I'm serious, Viva.

00:01:10.007 --> 00:01:12.076
Bridget, my best friend
I was telling you about,

00:01:12.212 --> 00:01:13.679
she's a Bergen.

00:01:13.814 --> 00:01:15.612
Look. Bridget and I do
a million fun things together.

00:01:15.747 --> 00:01:18.053
We talk and we play games
and we sing songs

00:01:18.189 --> 00:01:19.986
and make up
these really bad dances.

00:01:20.122 --> 00:01:21.855
It's a lot like...

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.085
Well, actually, it's a lot like
what you and I have been doing.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:26.787
The world's a lot different
than it used to be.

00:01:26.923 --> 00:01:29.528
Viva, look, I used to be
just like you.

00:01:29.663 --> 00:01:31.999
I built a bunker,
and I lived in it for years

00:01:32.134 --> 00:01:33.496
because I knew it was safe.

00:01:33.631 --> 00:01:36.465
And, sure, it-it kept me alive,

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:39.975
and I never had to wear pants,

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:43.812
but I was living without pants.

00:01:43.947 --> 00:01:44.977
Does that make sense?

00:01:45.113 --> 00:01:47.075
Well, I feel judged.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.050
You don't understand.
I just got my sister back.

00:01:50.185 --> 00:01:52.016
I'm not gonna lose you.

00:01:52.152 --> 00:01:54.289
For anything.

00:01:57.287 --> 00:01:58.589
Clay?

00:01:58.725 --> 00:02:01.725
I'm sorry, Viva,
but we have to leave.

00:02:01.861 --> 00:02:04.530
I don't want to lose
my brother, either.

00:02:06.837 --> 00:02:08.171
Let's move!

00:02:09.005 --> 00:02:11.900
No. No, Poppy, wait!

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:15.171
(gasps)

00:02:15.307 --> 00:02:17.741
Poppy, please!

00:02:18.608 --> 00:02:20.376
I want you to stay.

00:02:20.512 --> 00:02:22.279
Viva, I can't do that.

00:02:22.414 --> 00:02:23.879
But you can come with us.

00:02:24.015 --> 00:02:26.251
And I know you think it's risky,
and maybe it is,

00:02:26.386 --> 00:02:28.153
but it'll be worth it.

00:02:28.289 --> 00:02:30.358
Family's always worth it.

00:02:32.763 --> 00:02:34.959
No, no, no, I...

00:02:35.095 --> 00:02:36.298
I can't.

00:02:41.332 --> 00:02:43.734
♪ ♪

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:03.659
- (knocking at door)
- CREW MEMBER: Knock, knock.

00:03:03.794 --> 00:03:04.859
Almost showtime.

00:03:04.995 --> 00:03:06.994
Ugh. No sign of BroZone?

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:09.259
No, but I have an idea.

00:03:09.394 --> 00:03:11.997
We could practice.

00:03:12.132 --> 00:03:15.801
(laughs) I want to be famous,
but I'm not gonna work for it.

00:03:15.937 --> 00:03:17.164
Ew.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.204
Come on. We used to make up
little dances together

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.535
all the time, remember?

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.305
Hip, hip. Twist, flip.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.674
Our dances sucked.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.474
How many fans
do you think we can get

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:27.276
making up sucky dances?

00:03:27.411 --> 00:03:28.850
Hey, hello.

00:03:28.986 --> 00:03:31.016
Hello in there. Wake up.

00:03:31.151 --> 00:03:32.855
Wakey-wakey. Oh.

00:03:32.991 --> 00:03:34.223
He's dead? Oh, man.

00:03:34.359 --> 00:03:35.955
(hyperventilating):
What have we done?

00:03:36.091 --> 00:03:37.655
What do we do?

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:39.795
You remember the goldfish
you had as a kid?

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:41.363
You mean Sparkles?

00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:44.364
Mm-kay. Goodbye, little guy.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:45.696
VELVET:
Please hurry up and flush.

00:03:45.831 --> 00:03:47.368
Being this close to you
next to a toilet

00:03:47.503 --> 00:03:49.470
- makes me uncomfortable.
- (Floyd grunts)

00:03:51.101 --> 00:03:53.673
Wow. I thought ghosts
just floated away.

00:03:53.808 --> 00:03:55.471
Well, don't just stand there.
Go get him!

00:03:55.607 --> 00:03:56.873
Why does it have to be me?

00:03:57.008 --> 00:03:58.547
Because Crimp's locked
in the closet.

00:03:58.683 --> 00:03:59.541
Now, go!

00:03:59.677 --> 00:04:01.550
FLOYD:
Help! Help!

00:04:02.586 --> 00:04:04.346
- Help me, please.
- (music blares over headphones)

00:04:04.482 --> 00:04:05.720
(Veneer yelps)

00:04:05.855 --> 00:04:07.052
Help!

00:04:07.187 --> 00:04:09.721
♪ ♪

00:04:10.556 --> 00:04:12.822
- Gotcha.
- (Floyd panting)

00:04:12.958 --> 00:04:15.362
Please, Veneer,
just let me run past you.

00:04:15.497 --> 00:04:17.198
You can pretend
you never saw me.

00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:18.961
It-it'll be our little secret.

00:04:20.068 --> 00:04:21.069
I can't.

00:04:21.205 --> 00:04:23.898
I know. Velvet would kill you.

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:25.839
But just because
she's your sister

00:04:25.975 --> 00:04:28.773
doesn't mean you should let her
treat you like garbage.

00:04:29.609 --> 00:04:31.140
- Doesn't it?
- No.

00:04:31.276 --> 00:04:33.943
Sibling or not, you deserve
to be treated with kindness

00:04:34.079 --> 00:04:36.217
and to be around people
who would never try

00:04:36.352 --> 00:04:38.218
to change the you that you are.

00:04:38.353 --> 00:04:40.019
VELVET:
You got him.

00:04:40.154 --> 00:04:46.121
Hey, I know I probably don't
say this enough, but good job.

00:04:46.256 --> 00:04:49.090
We really make a great team,
don't we, bro?

00:04:51.527 --> 00:04:54.135
Now, come on. We should also
probably hire a new assistant,

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.204
which feels like a you job.

00:04:56.339 --> 00:04:59.338
Crimp! Hire us a new assistant!

00:04:59.473 --> 00:05:01.474
CRIMP:
I'm on it.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:04.946
(BroZone vocalizing
"Perfect" intro)

00:05:05.081 --> 00:05:07.350
♪ BroZone ♪

00:05:10.117 --> 00:05:12.551
♪ There ain't no stopping us,
stopping us ♪

00:05:12.686 --> 00:05:14.521
♪ We ain't pressing rewind ♪

00:05:14.656 --> 00:05:17.024
- ♪ Rewind ♪
- ♪ Rewind ♪

00:05:17.159 --> 00:05:18.423
♪ Rewind ♪

00:05:18.558 --> 00:05:19.956
♪ The sky was the limit ♪

00:05:20.091 --> 00:05:21.860
♪ Now the stars
where we livin' ♪

00:05:21.995 --> 00:05:24.297
♪ It's the vibe
when we're in it ♪

00:05:24.433 --> 00:05:26.029
♪ It'll blow your mind ♪

00:05:26.164 --> 00:05:28.498
♪ It's so perfect,
perfect, perfect ♪

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:31.173
♪ Harmony so cold ♪

00:05:31.309 --> 00:05:32.606
♪ Perfect, perfect, perfect ♪

00:05:32.741 --> 00:05:34.473
- (screams excitedly)
- ♪ Let it go ♪

00:05:34.608 --> 00:05:37.177
(harmonizing):
♪ Go... ♪

00:05:37.312 --> 00:05:39.280
Stop. Stop. Time-out.

00:05:39.416 --> 00:05:40.713
Let's do it again from the top.

00:05:40.848 --> 00:05:42.477
Spruce, I want some smolder
in those eyes.

00:05:42.612 --> 00:05:45.120
Clay, you're being too stiff.
We need some sillier robot.

00:05:45.255 --> 00:05:46.852
Bitty B, maybe a smaller diaper.

00:05:46.987 --> 00:05:48.821
If this diaper was any smaller,
I could taste it.

00:05:48.956 --> 00:05:50.852
That's why I don't wear
one of those.

00:05:50.987 --> 00:05:52.992
It's a hard fit to pull off.

00:05:53.128 --> 00:05:55.495
Really great note, John Dory.
Super helpful. Thanks. Thanks.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.294
Now I have
a creative note for you.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:58.529
Stop being bossy!

00:05:58.665 --> 00:06:00.094
What? I'm not being bossy.

00:06:00.229 --> 00:06:02.164
- I'm helping us be better.
- No.

00:06:02.299 --> 00:06:04.039
No, dude, you're forcing us
to be perfect,

00:06:04.175 --> 00:06:05.474
just like you always have,

00:06:05.609 --> 00:06:07.073
so we can hit
the perfect family harmony.

00:06:07.208 --> 00:06:08.610
Yeah, for Floyd.

00:06:08.745 --> 00:06:10.542
Is it, or is this all just
so you can tell people

00:06:10.677 --> 00:06:12.142
- what to do again?
- Wh-What?

00:06:12.277 --> 00:06:13.710
Guys, guys, this really isn't
helpful right now.

00:06:13.846 --> 00:06:15.210
Let's all maybe take five, huh?

00:06:15.345 --> 00:06:16.711
This isn't gonna work
if you keep on being

00:06:16.847 --> 00:06:18.053
the same old John Dory.

00:06:18.189 --> 00:06:19.449
Yeah. We've all changed.

00:06:19.585 --> 00:06:20.852
Bruce settled down,

00:06:20.987 --> 00:06:23.191
Branch is slightly taller
with zero glasses,

00:06:23.326 --> 00:06:24.424
and I'm a licensed CPA.

00:06:24.559 --> 00:06:26.393
Put some respect
on my name, fool!

00:06:26.528 --> 00:06:27.958
Well, I'm not allowed to change.

00:06:28.094 --> 00:06:30.125
I'm the oldest.
I had to be the leader.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.798
You love bossing us around.
Just admit it.

00:06:32.933 --> 00:06:34.295
Why do you think I moved
to the middle of nowhere?

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.032
So I didn't have to be
in charge of anyone.

00:06:36.168 --> 00:06:38.633
Four little brothers is
a lot of responsibility.

00:06:38.769 --> 00:06:40.034
Why do you think I left?

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.142
So no one would treat me
like you did.

00:06:42.278 --> 00:06:43.440
You know what, Spruce...

00:06:43.575 --> 00:06:44.539
It's Bruce!

00:06:44.674 --> 00:06:45.909
Thank you, Clay.

00:06:46.045 --> 00:06:47.682
Guys, we can't forget
about Floyd.

00:06:47.818 --> 00:06:49.078
Look, Branch is right--
we're here for Floyd.

00:06:49.213 --> 00:06:50.813
Let's just get this done,
and we can go

00:06:50.948 --> 00:06:52.217
- our separate ways.
- Fine.

00:06:52.352 --> 00:06:53.717
Wait. What?

00:06:53.852 --> 00:06:55.757
What? The mission's the mission.

00:06:55.893 --> 00:06:57.621
(scoffs) You didn't think
we'd all live together

00:06:57.756 --> 00:06:59.055
when this was all over, did you?

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:01.997
Singing songs
and roasting marshmallows?

00:07:02.132 --> 00:07:03.560
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:07:03.695 --> 00:07:05.128
Is that funny to you?

00:07:05.264 --> 00:07:08.570
That I might want us
to actually be a family again?

00:07:10.274 --> 00:07:13.069
Tiny Diamond, pull over now.

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:16.305
(all grunt)

00:07:17.008 --> 00:07:19.075
(scoffs)
Don't be a baby, Branch.

00:07:19.909 --> 00:07:21.242
You're mad at him,

00:07:21.378 --> 00:07:23.652
but you guys do
the exact same thing to me.

00:07:23.788 --> 00:07:26.015
You all still treat me
like the baby of the family,

00:07:26.151 --> 00:07:28.554
but guess what,
I stopped being a baby

00:07:28.689 --> 00:07:30.388
the day you guys
walked out on me.

00:07:30.523 --> 00:07:32.127
'Cause I had to.

00:07:32.263 --> 00:07:33.562
Then Grandma got eaten,

00:07:33.697 --> 00:07:35.156
and there was no one else
to take care of me.

00:07:35.292 --> 00:07:38.798
This time,
I'm walking out on you.

